        "title": "5b. ZenStack/Postgres error translation",
        "content": "\n```ts\n// apps/api/tests/error-handling.test.ts\nimport { toErrorResponse } from \"../src/lib/errors\";\n\ndescribe(\"toErrorResponse\", () => {\n  it(\"maps PrismaClientKnownRequestError P2025 to NOT_FOUND\", () => { /* … */ });\n  it(\"maps PrismaClientKnownRequestError P2002 to CONFLICT\", () => { /* … */ });\n  it(\"maps PrismaClientKnownRequestError P2003 to INVALID_INPUT (FK violation)\", () => { /* … */ });\n  it(\"maps HttpError.notFound to 404 with NOT_FOUND code\", () => { /* … */ });\n  it(\"maps HttpError.forbidden to 403 with FORBIDDEN code\", () => { /* … */ });\n  it(\"never leaks SQL text in the response message\", () => {\n    const sqlError = new Error(\"syntax error at or near SELECT; column user.password_hash\");\n    const result = toErrorResponse(sqlError);\n    expect(result.error.message).not.toMatch(/password_hash|SELECT/i);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
