        "title": "Summary of Gaps",
        "content": "| Area | Severity | Tests Exist? |\n|------|----------|-------------|\n| WebSocket hub (rooms, broadcast, dedup) | High | None |\n| Rate limiter logic | High | None |\n| `POST /api/conversations/direct` | High | None |\n| `POST /api/uploads` (blocked types, size, rate) | High | None |\n| `GET /api/files/:id` (access, redirect, disposition) | High | None |\n| `GET /api/rtc/ice` (STUN/TURN output) | Medium | None |\n| Org lifecycle hooks (default group, member cleanup) | High | None |\n| Realtime plugin socket emissions | High | Indirect only |\n| Call signaling & lifecycle | High | None |\n| Storage presign functions | Medium | None |\n| Error translation layer (`toErrorResponse`) | Medium | None |\n| Reaction uniqueness policies | Medium | Partial |\n| CALL/SYSTEM message type enforcement | High | None |\n| Structural field immutability (post.groupId, etc.) | High | None |\n| Reminder job scheduling | Low | None |\n| Invitation flow (admin-only creation) | Medium | None |\n\nThe highest-priority additions are the org lifecycle hooks, the WebSocket hub, and the HTTP routes (`/api/conversations/direct`, `/api/uploads`, `/api/files/:id`) — these carry business logic with no safety net.",
